      "facts": [
        "Waiting does not lock a task's status. Waiting on is required when saving a task whose new Status is Waiting. It is not required merely because the task used to be Waiting; changing to another status clears that description.",
        "The coach does not receive field contents or validation-message text. It cannot know which field caused a failure from the page name or a generic error flag; ask for the displayed error when diagnosing.",
        "Saving or restoring an active presentation completes the generated Populate event record with one or more presentations task. Saving the final financial report completes the generated Complete the event financial closeout task. Receipt drafts leave it open."
      ],
      "guidance_rules": [
        {
          "id": "waiting-status-diagnosis",
          "modes": [
            "troubleshoot"
          ],
          "patterns": [
            "\\b(task|follow up)\\b",
            "\\bwaiting\\b",
            "\\bstatus\\b",
            "\\b(change|changing|save|saving)\\b",
            "\\b(cannot|can t|unable|not|error|failed)\\b"
          ],
          "source": "manual-topic-work-queue-fast-actions-and-record-level-work",
          "message": "Waiting does not lock the task’s status. Waiting On is required only when the status you are saving is Waiting. When you change to another status, that description is cleared. I cannot see the form values or the validation message, so I cannot identify the cause of this failure yet.",
          "question": "What exact error does MOED show when you save? Copy its text and any field label; if no error appears, say so and describe what happens instead."
        },
        {
          "id": "leave-waiting",
          "modes": [
            "perform"
          ],
          "patterns": [
            "\\b(task|follow up)\\b",
            "\\bstatus\\b",
            "\\b(change|move|set|switch)\\b",
            "\\b(from waiting|to completed|to complete|to open|to in progress|to canceled)\\b"
          ],
          "source": "manual-topic-work-queue-fast-actions-and-record-level-work",
          "message": "1. Open the intended task using Edit Task.\n2. In Status, select the intended status. Waiting On is required only if the new status is Waiting; you do not need to fill it before switching to another status.\n3. Select Save Changes and check the saved status. Completing a task does not archive it.",
          "on_pages": {
            "edit_task.php": "1. You are already in Edit Task. In Status, choose the status you want to save.\n2. Waiting On is required only if the new status is Waiting; it is cleared when another status is saved.\n3. Select Save Changes and check the saved status. Completing a task does not archive it.",
            "add_task.php": "1. You are in the New Task form. In Status, choose the status you want to save.\n2. Waiting On is required only if the new status is Waiting; it is cleared when another status is saved.\n3. Finish the required task details, then select Add task and check the created task. This draft does not have an Edit Task action yet."
          },
          "question": ""
        }
      ]
    },
